## What Is a 1 Carat Asscher Cut Diamond Ring?

A 1 carat asscher cut diamond ring puts a square step-cut diamond in a setting sized for its unique octagonal outline and geometric step facets. The 1 carat asscher cut diamond ring is one of the most distinctive engagement ring options on the market — elegant, architectural, and completely different from brilliant-cut shapes.

The asscher cut was patented in 1902 by Joseph Asscher of Amsterdam. Unlike round brilliants designed to scatter light, the asscher is designed to create depth.

Its 72-facet configuration produces the signature concentric-square "windmill" pattern that makes the stone look like a hall of mirrors when you look straight down. That depth is what buyers love — and it is what makes the shape uniquely demanding on clarity and color.

[![1 carat asscher cut diamond ring solitaire collection in rose gold, white gold, and yellow gold](/images/asscher-cut-diamond-ring-solitaire-collection-rose-white-yellow-gold.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/asscher-cut-diamond-rings?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

I'm **Farzana Hasan**, a GIA-Certified Diamond Expert. The asscher cut has a specific set of requirements that brilliant cuts simply don't have.

Its step facets expose clarity and color in ways that change which grades you can safely buy. Most buyers discover these requirements after they've already made their purchase — that's why this post exists.

Full credentials and methodology at **[Diamond Critics](https://diamondcritics.com/about-farzana/)**.

