## 3 Mistakes 1 Carat Asscher Cut Diamond Ring Buyers Always Make

These are the 3 mistakes that cost buyers money or result in a ring they regret. Avoid all three before you look at a single stone.

### Mistake 1: Buying VS2 Clarity

VS2 is eye-clean in most brilliant cuts. In an asscher cut, it often is not.

Asscher's step facets run in long parallel lines across the stone. Those facets act like mirrors in a corridor.

An inclusion that sits inside the stone gets reflected — you see it directly, then again in the next mirror, then again in the one after that. A VS2 feather that would disappear in a round brilliant can look like a visible SI1 in an asscher.

This is why every experienced gemologist gives asscher buyers a VS1 floor. You can sometimes find a VS2 asscher that is eye-clean — but you have to inspect that specific stone under magnification and face-up in natural light before buying. Never order a VS2 asscher without a video.

The price difference between VS2 and VS1 in 1ct asschers is real but not enormous. A [1ct E-VS1 at $2,464](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28919719?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) costs more than a VS2 equivalent — but the VS2 risk is not worth the savings when the step facets will expose it.

[![Asscher cut diamond ring in yellow gold plain solitaire setting worn on model's finger](/images/asscher-cut-diamond-ring-yellow-gold-solitaire-on-finger.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/asscher-cut-diamond-rings?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

### Mistake 2: Forgetting the Setting Budget

Most buyers spend weeks researching their stone. They pick a grade, find a stone, and calculate their budget around it. Then they go to buy a ring setting and discover it costs $860 to $1,800 on top.

The 1 carat asscher cut diamond ring is a complete ring — stone plus setting. The stone is never the complete cost.

The [Ten Prong Solitaire in white gold is $860](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), the [Cathedral Solitaire in yellow gold is $1,240](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/tapered-cathedral-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-203288?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), and the [Art Deco vintage ring is $1,190](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-inspired-fleur-de-lis-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-315298?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — every setting adds a real number to your budget. None of these costs are optional.

Plan The Total Ring Number first. Decide your complete ring budget, then subtract the setting cost. The remainder is your stone budget.

[![Asscher cut diamond ring in yellow gold worn on hand with bracelets lifestyle shot](/images/asscher-cut-diamond-ring-yellow-gold-lifestyle-hands.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/asscher-cut-diamond-rings?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

### Mistake 3: Going Below G Color

Asscher cuts show color more clearly than brilliant cuts. The same long step facets that expose inclusions also reflect any yellow or warm tint in the stone.

In a round brilliant, color is broken up by 58 small facets firing in every direction. A G or H looks nearly identical to a D or E once it's in a ring.

In an asscher, the broad flat facets give you an unobstructed view straight into the stone. I or J color in an asscher looks noticeably warm — especially in white gold or platinum where the metal amplifies any warmth.

G is the safe minimum for asscher cuts in white metal. F or E is better. In yellow gold, you can sometimes go to H and the warm metal hides the stone's tint — but G is still the safer floor.

[![Asscher cut diamond ring with pear side stones in rose gold three-stone setting](/images/asscher-cut-diamond-three-stone-ring-rose-gold-pear-side-stones.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/asscher-cut-diamond-rings?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

