## The Total Ring Number

Every 1 carat asscher cut diamond ring has a Total Ring Number: the stone price plus the setting price. That is the actual cost of the ring. Most buyers only see the stone half of that number until they reach checkout.

Knowing The Total Ring Number before you shop changes how you budget. You start with your complete ring number, subtract the setting cost, and the remainder becomes your stone budget.

That order prevents the most common budget overrun in engagement ring shopping. Most buyers do it backwards — they fall in love with a stone, then discover the setting costs $1,000 on top.

