## Setting Styles for a 1 Carat Asscher Cut Diamond Ring

The asscher cut was designed in 1902 by Joseph Asscher. It became the defining stone of the Art Deco movement in the 1920s. The settings that work best with it are the ones that honor that geometric, architectural heritage.

Not every setting works. Here are the five styles ranked by how well they suit the asscher cut's shape.

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Rank</th><th>Setting</th><th>Price</th><th>Style</th><th>Asscher Fit</th><th>What This Means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>#1</td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-inspired-fleur-de-lis-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-315298?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">Art Deco Fleur-De-Lis WG</a></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-inspired-fleur-de-lis-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-315298?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$1,190</a></td><td>Vintage Art Deco pavé</td><td>Perfect — designed for this era</td><td>Best overall match for the asscher's 1920s character</td></tr><tr><td>#2</td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/tapered-cathedral-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-203288?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">Tapered Cathedral Solitaire YG</a></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/tapered-cathedral-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-203288?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$1,240</a></td><td>Elevated solitaire</td><td>Excellent — clean arch suits geometric stone</td><td>Formal, elevated, timeless — no competing elements</td></tr><tr><td>#3</td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">Ten Prong Solitaire WG</a></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$860</a></td><td>Clean solitaire</td><td>Excellent — prongs hold octagonal outline cleanly</td><td>Best price, most modern, lets the stone lead</td></tr><tr><td>#4</td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/petite-hidden-halo-solitaire-plus-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-192506?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">Petite Hidden Halo YG</a></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/petite-hidden-halo-solitaire-plus-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-192506?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$1,255</a></td><td>Hidden halo solitaire</td><td>Good — halo is below stone, outline stays intact</td><td>Extra sparkle without violating the geometric outline</td></tr><tr><td>#5</td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-inspired-fleur-de-lis-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-by-james-allen-item-315297?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">Art Deco Fleur-De-Lis RG</a></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-inspired-fleur-de-lis-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-by-james-allen-item-315297?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$1,190</a></td><td>Vintage Art Deco rose gold</td><td>Excellent — rose gold softens geometric edges</td><td>Romantic vintage look — same Art Deco detail, warmer metal</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** The Art Deco Fleur-De-Lis setting ranks #1 because it is the natural stylistic home of the asscher cut. This stone was the centerpiece of Art Deco jewelry in the 1920s — a setting designed for that era suits it perfectly. The Ten Prong Solitaire is the best choice if you want a clean modern look at the lowest setting price.

### Solitaire Settings

The solitaire is the most faithful setting for a 1 carat asscher cut diamond ring. It lets the stone's geometry take the lead without any competing design elements.

The [Ten Prong Solitaire in white gold at $860](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) holds the asscher's octagonal girdle cleanly. The prongs are positioned at the eight corners. The stone sits elevated, showing the step facets at full depth.

Yellow gold and rose gold versions are available at the same $860 price — [yellow gold here](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-by-james-allen-item-311236?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) and [rose gold here](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-by-james-allen-item-311237?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

The [Tapered Cathedral Solitaire in yellow gold at $1,240](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/tapered-cathedral-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-203288?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) adds the cathedral arch — the shank curves up and elevates the stone like a gothic arch. The architectural quality of that setting matches the architectural quality of the asscher cut directly.

[![Asscher cut diamond ring rose gold channel split band round diamonds model lifestyle](/images/asscher-cut-diamond-ring-rose-gold-channel-split-band-model.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/asscher-cut-diamond-rings?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

### Art Deco and Vintage Settings

The asscher cut's Art Deco heritage makes vintage-style settings the most authentic choice for this ring.

The [Art Deco Fleur-De-Lis Pavé Vintage-Style setting in white gold at $1,190](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-inspired-fleur-de-lis-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-315298?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) has pavé shoulders, filigree-style detailing, and a square basket that frames the asscher's octagonal outline. The [rose gold version at the same $1,190](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-inspired-fleur-de-lis-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-by-james-allen-item-315297?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) softens the geometric edges with warm metal.

Both of these settings paired with the [GIA 1.00ct E-VS1 at $2,464](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28919719?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) give you the full asscher experience — the stone, the setting style, and the total ring — for $3,654.

[![Asscher cut diamond ring yellow gold full halo round diamond pavé band engagement ring](/images/asscher-cut-diamond-ring-yellow-gold-halo-pave-band.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/asscher-cut-diamond-rings?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

### Hidden Halo Settings

A standard round pavé halo is not recommended for asscher cuts. The circle fights the rectangle. But the hidden halo works differently.

The [Petite Hidden Halo Solitaire Plus in yellow gold at $1,255](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/petite-hidden-halo-solitaire-plus-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-192506?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) places the melee diamonds below the center stone's table, not around it at the same level. From above, the asscher's octagonal outline is completely intact. The extra sparkle is only visible from the side and in profile.

Paired with the [GIA 1.00ct F-VS1 at $2,521](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29365844?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), the total ring is $3,776. If you want halo sparkle without compromising the asscher's clean geometric outline, this is the only halo setting that works for this shape.

---

## Metal Choice for a 1 Carat Asscher Cut Diamond Ring

Metal choice affects how the asscher cut reads color — and that matters more for this shape than for brilliant cuts.

**White gold and platinum** are the neutral choice — they do not add any warm tint to the stone's appearance. If you are buying G or E color, white gold will show the stone at its full grade. The [Ten Prong Solitaire in white gold](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311235?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) and the [Art Deco Fleur-De-Lis in white gold](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-inspired-fleur-de-lis-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-315298?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) are both at their best with G or better stones.

**Yellow gold** reflects warm light into the asscher's step facets. This can make an H color look warmer than it is — but it also means you can sometimes drop to H and have the yellow gold carry the warmth naturally. The [Cathedral Solitaire in yellow gold at $1,240](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/tapered-cathedral-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-203288?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the most historically accurate setting for an asscher in warm metal — the Art Deco movement used yellow gold heavily.

[![Asscher cut diamond ring yellow gold halo setting worn on model's hand lifestyle shot](/images/asscher-cut-diamond-ring-yellow-gold-halo-model.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/asscher-cut-diamond-rings?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

**Rose gold** is the most flattering metal for buyers who want warmth without committing to yellow. The [Art Deco Fleur-De-Lis in rose gold at $1,190](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-inspired-fleur-de-lis-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-by-james-allen-item-315297?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) pairs especially well with F or G stones — the rose gold adds romantic warmth while the stone remains visually clean.

Platinum is the premium choice for white metal. The [Ten Prong Solitaire in platinum at $1,200](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/ten-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-by-james-allen-item-311240?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is slightly more than the 14k white gold version but adds long-term durability for a ring that will be worn daily.

Platinum does not need rhodium re-plating over time the way white gold does. For a ring centered on a step-cut stone where metal appearance matters — because the asscher's open step facets reflect the band — platinum's consistent white color is worth the small premium over 14k white gold.

